const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文在区分条件波动率预测和简单已实现波动率代理后，检验预期收益是否与特质风险相关。 阅读时应将其放回原始样本、时点和制度环境中理解，不能把问题本身当作跨市场结论。",en:"The article studies whether expected returns relate to idiosyncratic risk after distinguishing predictable conditional volatility from a simple realized-volatility proxy. Read it as a bounded question, not as a conclusion that automatically travels beyond its sample, dates, or institutional setting."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2008.02.003",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Economics · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Economics · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"它在资产定价框架中估计公司层面的波动率，并比较不同波动率度量下的收益关系，因此因子模型、预测设定和持有窗口都很关键。 比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系共同构成研究合同；改变其中任一选择，可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"It estimates firm-level volatility within an asset-pricing framework and compares return relations across volatility measures, so the factor model, forecast specification, and holding window matter. The comparison, observation window, and control relation are part of the research contract; changing one can change the proposition being tested."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2008.02.003",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Economics · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Economics · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"需要清洗后的日收益、无风险和因子序列、证券标识、退市、交易状态、波动率估计窗口以及带日期的样本范围。 字段定义、可得时点和样本筛选必须与原研究分开记录，不能因变量同名或使用最新修订值便视为可比。",en:"A comparable analysis needs cleaned daily returns, risk-free and factor series, security identifiers, delistings, trading-status flags, volatility-estimation windows, and dated universe rules. Keep fields, availability timing, and sample filters separate from the original study: a same-named variable or later-revised database is not automatically comparable."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2008.02.003",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Economics · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Economics · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"来源研究的是特质风险度量选择如何改变横截面关系，并未说明原始波动率是普遍被定价的因子。 它只支持来源描述的经验或理论关系，不能把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"The source investigates how the chosen measure of idiosyncratic risk changes the cross-sectional relation; it does not establish that raw volatility is a universal priced factor. This remains the empirical or theoretical relation described by the source; it does not turn association, fit, or historical performance into causality, an executable procedure, or a future guarantee."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2008.02.003",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Economics · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Economics · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"声明因子模型和波动率预测；保留停滞价格与低频交易；固定再平衡与收益期限；检验样本和微盘过滤的敏感性。 开展后续分析前，应将这些选择写入版本化研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"State the factor model and volatility forecast; keep stale prices and infrequent trading visible; preserve rebalancing and return horizons; and test sensitivity to sample and microcap filters. Before extending the analysis, record these choices in a versioned note and retain the primary-source link and access date."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2008.02.003",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Economics · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Economics · DOI record · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 Journal of Financial Economics · DOI record。模型依赖的波动率估计及其市场时期不能转化为当前风险评分、因果判断或另一市场的可交易预测。 如需数值结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites Journal of Financial Economics · DOI record. Model-dependent volatility estimates and the paper's market period cannot be converted into a current risk score, a causal claim, or an investable prediction for another venue. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2008.02.003",label:{zh:"Journal of Financial Economics · DOI record · 来源说明",en:"Journal of Financial Economics · DOI record · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Idiosyncratic Risk and the Cross-Section of Expected Stock Returns”公开说明的研究对象、设计与适用边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。模型依赖的波动率估计及其市场时期不能转化为当前风险评分、因果判断或另一市场的可交易预测。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Idiosyncratic Risk and the Cross-Section of Expected Stock Returns”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
